      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Opponents of reparations often argue that it is economically unfeasible for the US government to fund such a massive program, claiming it would create a \"two-tiered society\" based on race. They frequently contend that the concept of reparations is fundamentally flawed because slavery ended over 150 years ago, and therefore, the government has no legal or moral obligation to compensate descendants of those who were enslaved. Furthermore, critics argue that focusing on race-based compensation ignores the complex, individual circumstances of poverty and inequality that affect people of all backgrounds today.",
